From: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi7: fix cac_required field hidden behind CONFIG_MAP_SUPPORT

struct wifi_dev's cac_required member is wrapped in
"#ifdef CONFIG_MAP_SUPPORT", but the field is DFS/CAC state used by
non-MAP code paths too:

  - rt_channel.c mtk_cfg80211_vndr_cmd_set_channel_attributes handles
    MTK_CFG80211_CHAN_SET_FLAG_CAC_REQUIRED unconditionally and writes
    wdev.cac_required (always compiled in AP mode);
  - cmm_rdm_mt.c DfsZwBypassCac reads wdev.cac_required under
    "#if defined(MT_DFS_SUPPORT)".

With CONFIG_MAP_SUPPORT left off (default in the OpenWrt Kconfig),
every TU using the field fails with:

  error: 'struct wifi_dev' has no member named 'cac_required'

Move the single UCHAR field out of the CONFIG_MAP_SUPPORT guard so it
is always present; MAPCfg, dev_role and cac_capability stay guarded.
CAC_REQUIRED_* (mt_rdm.h) are already defined unconditionally.

diff --git a/mt_wifi/include/rtmp.h b/mt_wifi/include/rtmp.h
index b147465..2a309b2 100644
--- a/mt_wifi/include/rtmp.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/rtmp.h
@@ -2832,13 +2832,17 @@ struct wifi_dev {
 	UCHAR quick_ch_change;
 #ifdef CONFIG_MAP_SUPPORT
 	MAP_CONFIG MAPCfg;
-	UCHAR cac_required;
 
 	UCHAR dev_role;
 #ifdef DFS_CAC_R2
 	struct cac_capability_lib cac_capability;
 #endif
 #endif
+	/* cac_required is DFS/CAC state used outside the MAP feature too:
+	 * rt_channel.c (MTK_CFG80211_CHAN_SET_FLAG_CAC_REQUIRED vendor cmd) and
+	 * cmm_rdm_mt.c DfsZwBypassCac (compiled under MT_DFS_SUPPORT). Keep the
+	 * field outside the CONFIG_MAP_SUPPORT guard so non-MAP builds compile. */
+	UCHAR cac_required;
 	UINT8 auto_channel_cen_ch_2;
 	BOOLEAN is_marvell_ap;
 	VOID *pDot11_H;
